WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:06.270
We've met up with Colin Au in the new cruise
boat his company commissioned and built to

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.910
carry passengers from the Rhine to the Danube.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.400
The Asian manager has considerable experience
in Europe.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.700
"I was born in Malaysia which was a British
colony at that time.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.590
So most people go to studies in England.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.220
I wanted to be engineer.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.170
So I studied at the university of Birmingham.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.860
Chemical engineering.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.309
And after that decided to do my business studies.

00:00:32.309 --> 00:00:34.440
That is when I went to America."

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:41.159
For now, Colin Au can give his interviews
in any of the 55 cabins, but soon Genting

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.920
Hong Kong's riverboats will be on the water.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.440
The traditional drum roll when the keel is
laid for a new boat is a festive occasion.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.659
What's more, the new Asian owner is beefing
up the operation, which is good news for

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:00.699
the regional economy.

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:04.659
Last year Genting bought three German shipyards
on the Baltic coast.

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:07.890
Together, they make up the MV Werften company.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.060
It has a workforce of about 1,500 -- and it's
hiring.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:20.120
"We intend to build ten global class, very
large ships, plus also river ships and also

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.380
expedition yachts.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:29.900
Over the next ten years - maybe about 15 billion
euros in terms of new ships."

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:36.620
Genting Hong Kong spent 230 million euros
buying up this yard in Wismar and the two

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.820
others, in Warnemünde and Stralsund.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.420
Other overseas investors had shown interest
in the yards.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.000
But nothing ever came of it.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:51.020
What's unusual about the situation here is that Genting, one of the world's largest cruise ship

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.540
operators is commissioning ships for its
own use.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.560
Colin Au shows us photos of the vessels he's
planning to build.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.480
Rhine river yachts like this one.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:11.799
Robust expedition vessels for trips to the
North Pole, and huge cruise ships accommodating

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.220
up to 5,000 passengers.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.960
All to be built at Genting's German shipyards.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:22.120
"In the whole world there are now two companies
that can build cruise ships: Meyer in Papenburg

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.480
and Turku in Finland.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.000
And Ficantiere in Italy and France.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:34.100
Both shipyards, if you order a ship now, you
are waiting till 2024, 2025

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.940
which is too far away.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:43.240
So by buying our shipyards and building ships,
we can get our ships in 2020, which is much earlier.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:48.760
The Genting Group is perhaps best known for
developing and operating casinos and hotels

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:49.810
and resorts.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:53.080
It expanded into the cruise business in the
1990s.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.200
Many people, including people here in this
region of northeastern Germany, were surprised

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:03.030
that the Malaysian conglomerate, or rather
its Hong Kong subsidiary, chose to buy shipyards

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.080
in Europe.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.829
"Passenger ships are only successfully built
in Europe.

00:03:06.829 --> 00:03:12.840
And we must be close to the 800 to 900 subcontractors
that will be building our ships."

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.420
These coins from around the world are supposed
to bring luck.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:22.260
The ceremonial keel laying is a big moment
for the city of Wismar.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.960
The mayor is in attendance.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.840
"There's a wave of positivity rolling through
Wismar.

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:34.430
The city is growing.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.180
There's a lot of demand for real estate and
so on.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.700
There's a sense of excitement in the air."

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.200
Colin Au has been with Genting for decades.

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:50.779
The company appears to be here for the long
haul:

00:03:50.779 --> 00:03:53.760
And hopefully its gamble with German shipyards
will pay off.

